      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for prescription use of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the extra dose adds no analgesic benefit.\n\nThese options are within the labeled limits:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum daily dose.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day). This range is typical for pain or fever.\n\nPossible typos are 1600 mg as the total daily dose, which would be 400 mg four times daily, or 800 mg instead of 1600 mg.\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it. If you need more analgesia than the maximum dose gives, you could add acetaminophen or another agent. Ibuprofen should be taken with food, and a GI-protection plan may be worth considering for a longer course."
      }
